-- title:
--   Base change to ℚ̄ of the two chart rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $p$, an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ and an element $j_0 \in F_0$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $A$ a discrete valuation domain with $\operatorname{Frac} A = L$, such that the image of $p$ in $A$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) for the intermediate field of $L$ in $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(F_0)$, and similarly $\overline{F}$ for the corresponding subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$; $K$ is assumed to carry an $A$-algebra structure compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ and $\hat\jmath \in \overline{F}$ both have underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $j_0$, with $j \neq 0$ and $\hat\jmath \neq 0$, and fix compatible algebra maps $A \to L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume further (hypothesis `hmem`) that pushing coefficients forward along $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ carries every element of $K$ into $\overline{F}$. Then there exist $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra isomorphisms $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_A \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} \cong \mathcal{O}_{\overline{F},\{\hat\jmath\}}$ and $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_A \mathcal{O}_{\infty} \cong \mathcal{O}_{\overline{F},\{\hat\jmath^{-1}\}}$, where $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\mathcal{O}_{\infty}$ are the subalgebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively $A[j^{-1}]$, and the right-hand sides are the subalgebras of elements of $\overline{F}$ integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[\hat\jmath]$, respectively $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[\hat\jmath^{-1}]$; each isomorphism sends $1 \otimes b$ to the coefficientwise image of $b$ along $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This identifies the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the two affine chart rings of the two-chart integral model of a $q$-expansion field $L\cdot F_0$ over a discrete valuation ring $A$ with the corresponding chart rings computed directly over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the level being left arbitrary. It is used in the construction of the curve model for $X_1(p)$ and its comparison with the pullback of the chart at a point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_tensor_chartAlgFin_chartRing_and_chartAlgInf_laurentBaseChange_twoChartModel_of_coe_eq_coeffEmb.lean

